# Switch to a repository created from the picker

`enter` on the fresh-repository candidate should initialize the displayed
checkout, create its session, and switch the invoking client.

    :bins jj tmux cat sh sed mkdir

> [!NOTE]
> 'jj', 'tmux', 'cat', 'sh', 'sed', and 'mkdir' are available.

    :copy tests/fixtures/jjconfig.toml .jjconfig.toml (copied)
    :w .config/smth/smth.toml (written)

```toml
[repo]
root = "repos"

[tmux]
setup = ": > .smth-ready"
```

Reserve a destination and live names so the repository and plain candidates
have different names. Each must be disambiguated before it is displayed.

    :$ mkdir -p repos/switched~1 (exit: 0)
    :t new-session -d -s switched "cat" (success)
    :t new-session -d -s switched~2 "cat" (success)
    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :t resize-window -t runner:0 -x 120 -y 14 (success)
    :t respawn-pane -k -t runner:0.0 'smth --no-base; cat' (success)
    :pane runner:0.0
    :settle -d 2s (settled)

Existing matches remain the default selection. The repository candidate shows
`switched~3` and its destination, while the plain candidate shows `switched~1`.

    :k switched
    :snap

```terminal
session: switched
  2/3 | [C-r] repo: none | [C-x] close, [C-f] flag
   switched~3                               ~/r/switched~3                                                        repo ┃
   switched~1                                                                                                     tmux ┃
▌⬤ switched                                                                                                            │
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────








```

Navigate between both candidates, then select the repository to create.

    :k M-up
    :snap

```terminal
session: switched
  2/3 | [C-r] repo: none
▌  switched~3                               ~/r/switched~3                                                        repo ┃
   switched~1                                                                                                     tmux ┃
 ⬤ switched                                                                                                            │
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────








```

    :k down
    :snap

```terminal
session: switched
  2/3 | [C-r] repo: none
   switched~3                               ~/r/switched~3                                                        repo ┃
▌  switched~1                                                                                                     tmux ┃
 ⬤ switched                                                                                                            │
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────








```

    :k up
    :snap

```terminal
session: switched
  2/3 | [C-r] repo: none
▌  switched~3                               ~/r/switched~3                                                        repo ┃
   switched~1                                                                                                     tmux ┃
 ⬤ switched                                                                                                            │
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────








```

Synchronize on a persistent option written by a one-shot tmux hook after the
client changes session.

    :t set-hook -g client-session-changed "set-hook -gu client-session-changed; set-option -g @smth.test-switched yes" (success)
    :k enter
    :$ sh -c 'until test -f repos/switched~3/.smth-ready; do :; done' (exit: 0)
    :$ sh -c 'until test "$(tmux show-options -gqv @smth.test-switched)" = yes; do :; done' (exit: 0)

The client should show the new session after repository initialization and tmux
setup complete.

    :t display-message -p '#{client_session}' (success)

```
switched~3
```

    :$ sh -c 'test -d repos/switched~3/.jj && test -d repos/switched~3/.git && test ! -e repos/switched~1/.jj' (exit: 0)
    :$ sh -c 'tmux show-options -qv -t "=switched~3:" @smth.repo | sed "s#$PWD#<ROOT>#g"' (exit: 0)

```stdout
<ROOT>/repos/switched~3
```

    :t has-session -t '=switched' (success)
    :t has-session -t '=switched~2' (success)
    :t display-message -p -t runner:0.0 '#{pane_dead}' (success)

```
0
```

Selecting an existing live session should switch to it without initializing
a checkout, even when prospective repository and plain candidates are present.

    :t switch-client -t runner (success)
    :t new-session -d -s fallback -c '#{pane_start_path}' 'smth --no-base --query switched~2; cat' (success)
    :t resize-window -t fallback:0 -x 120 -y 14 (success)
    :pane fallback:0.0
    :settle -d 2s (settled)
    :snap

```terminal
session: switched~2
  1/5 | [C-r] repo: none | [C-x] close, [C-f] flag
   switched~2~1                             ~/r/switched~2~1                                                      repo ┃
   switched~2~1                                                                                                   tmux ┃
▌⬤ switched~2                                                                                                          ┃
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────








```

    :t set-hook -g client-session-changed "set-hook -gu client-session-changed; wait-for -S switched-existing" (success)
    :k enter
    :t wait-for switched-existing (success)
    :t display-message -p '#{client_session}' (success)

```
switched~2
```

    :$ sh -c 'test ! -e repos/switched~2 && test ! -e repos/switched~2~1' (exit: 0)

